description:
Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.
The community you will join:
Airbnb is seeking a Partnerships Enablement Intern to join the Partnerships &amp; Business Development team for France and Benelux for a 6-month internship.
The goal of our Partnerships &amp; Business Development team is to build from the ground up partnerships and alliances to support Airbnb’s business and growth. They are responsible for deal making and partners management from A to Z. Starting with sourcing stakeholders who could become partners tomorrow, to implementing the partnerships per se, all the while working to ensure successful, long-lasting relationships with all the stakeholders.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
The difference you will make:
You’ll be joining the team at a particularly exciting moment : we’re building our local strategy from the ground up, about to launch a major partnership, and driving an innovative new project. You’ll get 360° exposure to business development, with a strong focus on activation: event execution, stakeholder alignment, and impact tracking. It’s an opportunity to contribute to a high-impact launch, learn what great outcomes look like, and build the foundation to engage future partners with confidence.&nbsp;
You can expect to:
Partner with your mentor - Business Development Lead for France and Benelux - to oversee activation plans for ongoing partnerships
Contribute to event coordination: this involves planning, stakeholder management (both internally and externally), D-day activation, and last but not least, after-action review to guarantee solid measurement practices, feedback collection&nbsp; and suggest improvements
Participate in mapping out potential new partners in the region: you will turn into an investigator to seed out ideas for new partnerships to develop our business&nbsp;
&nbsp;
The intern experience:
As an intern, you’ll be integrated into a team where you’ll contribute to challenging projects. Your manager, team, and our incredible employee community will strive to be superhosts to you during your internship. We provide the support, mentorship, fun, and real world experience needed to accelerate your learning and make a real impact on our product, as Airbnb revolutionizes connection, belonging, and travel.
&nbsp;
Your expertise:
We welcome any candidate who is passionate about building long-lasting and effective partnerships! You are probably the right person for this role if you tick the following boxes:
You are in your final year of getting a Master’s degree&nbsp;
No preference for the area of study, but you have to be data- and tech-savvy&nbsp;
Ideally, you have previous experience in working in some partnership capacity. You were/are part of the student committee and stroke deals with the local partners for the benefits of your fellow students? We want to hear from you!&nbsp;
You speak both French and English very fluently (you don’t have to be a native speaker, but you need to be comfortable with both languages)
Based in Paris (this position requires in-person office presence, but our Paris office is absolutely gorgeous)&nbsp;
Desired Skills
Strong communication skills - Good knowledge of French market preferred&nbsp;
Skilled user of Excel/Google Sheets
Strong analytical skills and ability to derive high-quality analysis from data.&nbsp;
Ability to work proactively and results-driven: always trying to learn that extra detail that can help make the most accurate decisions
Experience with an internet marketplace business or within the travel industry is a plus
Curiosity is your driver, you are an avid learner and default to connecting with people to hear their story.&nbsp;
You are an authentic “people person” with the ability to connect the right people together. You default to thinking strategic and long-term rewards rather than only tactical, short-term success
Comfortable working with ambiguity
&nbsp;
Equal Employment Opportunity:
Airbnb values diversity &amp; belonging and is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. All individuals seeking employment at Airbnb are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, gender, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, or any other legally protected characteristic.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
How We'll Take Care of You:
The base pay range shown below is annualized, is subject to change and may be modified in the future.&nbsp; This role may also be eligible for benefits and Employee Travel Credits.&nbsp;
France Annual Pay Range
€25.000 &mdash; €25.000 EUR
&nbsp;
Reasonable Accommodations: We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.
A Note on Recruiting Scams: Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @ airbnb.com or @ ext.airbnb.com email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.
